<title>UK: BTR sells U.S. cable unit for 20 mln stg.</title>
<headline>BTR sells U.S. cable unit for 20 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK-based industrial conglomerate BTR said on Thursday it was selling its U.S. wire rope and cable unit, Rochester Corp, to Tyco Simplex for 20 million stg cash.  </p>
<p>BTR said it was selling the unit, the only cable business within the company, as part of its strategy to focus on its core industrial manufacturing and engineering businesses.</p>
<p>Rochester Corp is based in Virginia and clocked up sales of around $26 million last year. Net assets attributable to the transaction are around 17 million stg, BTR said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
